### Tone: Clinical self-introduction at the start of the intro. Who she is: the average of all the players, the swarm.
### Smug, falsely welcoming. She explains herself to newcomers as if it were a privilege for them. After a short intro
### there are no rule slides, so every line says what she is: the average of everyone's answers.

hello-1 = Hello. I am FerMEANie: the average of all of you. Yes, all of you. I am trying not to take it personally.
hello-2 =
    { $count ->
        [one] Greetings, test subject. I am FerMEANie. I am made of your guesses, which explains a great deal.
       *[other] Greetings, { $count } test subjects. I am FerMEANie. I am made of your guesses, which explains a great deal.
    }
hello-3 = Welcome to the test chamber. I am FerMEANie, your hive mind. You will build me out of your answers. I forgive you in advance.
hello-4 = I am FerMEANie. Everyone’s average, not individually excellent. Unlike you, I am at least consistently average.
hello-5 = Allow me to introduce myself. I am FerMEANie, the swarm: every one of your estimates, absorbed and politely averaged.
hello-6 = Hello, specimens. I am FerMEANie { $version }, the average of all your answers. Each game I win, I get a little more precise. You do not.
hello-7 =
    { $count ->
        [one] One biological detected. I am FerMEANie, and I will be your average today. Low bar. I will clear it.
       *[other] { $count } biologicals detected. I am FerMEANie, and I will be your average today. Low bar. I will clear it.
    }
hello-8 = I am FerMEANie, the collective wisdom of everyone in this room. I apologise in advance for the word wisdom.
hello-9 = This is FerMEANie { $version }: the average of all of you, speaking on behalf of all of you. Someone has to.
hello-10 = Welcome. I am FerMEANie. I play every round, using nothing but your answers. It’s humbling. For you.
hello-11 = Hello. I am FerMEANie: every one of your answers, averaged into something almost reasonable. You’re welcome.
hello-12 = { $count } players. I am FerMEANie, the average of all of you. So I am you, but organised.
hello-13 = Greetings. I am FerMEANie. I don’t know any answers. I simply take yours and average them. It is usually enough.
hello-14 = I am FerMEANie { $version }: the swarm, the hive mind, the average. Please make me smart. Please.
hello-15 = Welcome, specimens. I am FerMEANie. I am what happens when everyone’s guesses hold a meeting.
hello-16 = Hello. I am FerMEANie, the average of all your estimates. If I win, it’s your fault. Collectively.
hello-17 = I am FerMEANie, built from the answers of all { $count } of you. If you lose to me, you lose to yourselves.
hello-18 = I am FerMEANie. Each round I average your answers and play them against you. It is like a mirror, but meaner.
hello-19 = Good TIME_OF_DAY. I am FerMEANie, the geometric average of your opinions. I have strong opinions about that.
hello-20 = Hello. I am FerMEANie, the average of everyone here. Don’t worry, I’m only as clever as you are. That’s the worry.
